    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nConsider the following:\n\n``` lua\nx = (\n   y = ( 123 )\n-- ^ cursor here, on 'y'\n)\n```\n\nIn stock vim/Neovim, `viB` would select inside the outer block, while mini.ai selects inside the inner block, i.e. the next block on the current line.\n\nI'd love to have some slightly more granular search options to support more native-style behaviour, e.g:\n\n* `cover_then_next`: First look for surrounding context, then next\n* `next_then_cover`: Equivalent to the current `cover_or_next` \n* ... And perhaps so on for the other `_{prev|nearest}` search methods.\n\nThank you for the great work on mini.nvim! ",
